    <string name="diag_hint_http_unreachable">Check that the controller is powered, on the same network, and that its HTTP port is correct. Guest Wi-Fi and client isolation block access.</string>
    <string name="diag_hint_http_timeout">The controller did not answer in time. Move closer to the access point or check for a busy controller.</string>
    <string name="diag_hint_http_error">Open the WLED web UI in a browser. A password or a disabled JSON API can cause this.</string>
    <string name="diag_hint_http_bad_json">The response is not WLED JSON. Verify the address and port; another device may be using that IP.</string>
    <string name="diag_hint_udp_send_failed">UDP may be blocked by the network. Test HTTP first, then try DDP on port 4048 and WLED UDP on 21324.</string>
    <string name="diag_hint_unsupported_protocol">For more than 480 LEDs use DNRGB instead of DRGB, or switch to DDP.</string>
    <string name="diag_hint_projection_denied">Android requires explicit consent for every capture session. Start again and confirm the system dialog.</string>
    <string name="diag_hint_projection_stopped">The system or the user stopped the projection. Start a new session from the Ambilight screen.</string>
    <string name="diag_hint_black_frame">Protected video can be hidden from capture. Test with unprotected content; this app does not bypass DRM.</string>
    <string name="diag_hint_network_lost">The controller stopped answering. Check Wi-Fi, the controller power and its IP address; then test the device again.</string>
    <string name="diag_hint_led_mismatch">Set the same number of LEDs per side as configured in WLED (Settings → LED preferences).</string>
    <string name="diag_hint_config_corrupt">Damaged settings were replaced with defaults. Re-check devices and calibration.</string>
    <string name="diag_hint_discovery_unavailable">mDNS can be blocked. Add the controller manually or run the explicit network scan.</string>
    <string name="diag_hint_realtime_occupied">Another app or Hyperion may be sending realtime data. Stop it, or wait for the WLED timeout.</string>

